# Phase 1 Version 3: Full-History Structural Residual Graph MoE

Version 3 keeps the validated K=80 HGT as an indispensable base branch. Five
deterministic graph views provide structural residuals; they never replace or
remove the complete-history representation.

## Architecture

```text
K=80 complete causal history --------------------> h_full
                                                      |
five deterministic causal structural views -> h_1...h_5
                                                      |
Router(h_full, h_1, ..., h_5, task embedding)         |
                     |                                |
                     v                                v
       dense task-conditioned weights       structural residual adapters
                     |                                |
                     +------------> h_task = h_full + weighted residuals
                                                      |
                                             six Version 1 heads
```

The five views retain the Version 2 definitions:

| Expert | Event budget | Selection rule |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Short temporal | 10 | Last ten visible events |
| Possession | 20 | Backward team-control approximation |
| Spatial | 16 | Nearest events in the last 30 events |
| Actor relation | 18 | Recent events involving up to ten active players |
| Transition | 12 | Events around the latest team change or transition type |

Every branch ends at the same event `e_t`, excludes `e_(t+1)` and all future
events, and uses the same next-event target. The full branch always contains up
to 80 consecutive visible events.

## Shared HGT And Residuals

All six disconnected branches are encoded in one PyG batch by the same
two-layer, four-head, 64-channel HGT used by Version 1. For each structural
expert, the residual adapter observes:

```text
[h_full, h_expert, h_expert - h_full] -> 192 -> 16 -> 64
```

The final adapter layer is zero-initialized. Before residual training, all six
task contexts therefore equal `h_full`, independently of Router weights.

## Dense Router

For each prediction task, the Router jointly observes the complete post-HGT
state of all branches:

```text
[h_full, h_1, h_2, h_3, h_4, h_5, task_embedding]
                  400 -> 128 -> 5
```

Softmax is Dense over all five experts. Version 3 contains no Top-2 path and no
expert dropout. Conditional execution is deferred until a future implementation
can avoid constructing and encoding unselected branches.

## K=80 Lower Bound

The controlled run loads the Version 1 K=80 checkpoint and freezes its complete
HGT and six heads. Epoch 0 evaluates the zero-residual model and must reproduce
the recorded K=80 metrics within `1e-6`; otherwise training stops. Epoch 0 also
participates in best-checkpoint selection, so a harmful residual run cannot
replace the validated K=80 checkpoint.

Only residual adapters, task embeddings, and the Dense Router are optimized in
the first controlled experiment. The six-task loss and all target definitions
remain identical to Version 1.

## Controlled Protocol

```text
competition        = England
train matches      = 48
validation matches = 12
steps per match    = 96
epochs             = 8, plus epoch 0 equivalence evaluation
batch size         = 48
optimizer          = AdamW
learning rate      = 3e-4
weight decay       = 1e-4
seed               = 20260715
routing            = Dense only
```

## Reproduction

```bash
paper_1/Phase_1/.venv/bin/python \
  paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/scripts/run_residual_moe_experiment.py \
  --device cuda:0 \
  --output-dir paper_1/Phase_1/version_3/experiments/controlled_v1
```

Canonical outputs are `result.json`, `checkpoint.pt`, and
`comparison_with_version_1.json` under `experiments/controlled_v1`.

## Controlled Result

The single-seed validation run selected residual epoch 6:

| Metric | Version 1 K=80 | Version 3 | Difference |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Event Macro-F1 | 0.44647 | 0.45044 | +0.00397 |
| Event accuracy | 0.72743 | 0.73872 | +0.01128 |
| Time MAE (seconds) | 1.70069 | 1.69227 | -0.00842 |
| Position distance | 37.84345 | 37.82435 | -0.01910 |
| Acting-side accuracy | 0.83420 | 0.83941 | +0.00521 |
| Player Top-3 accuracy | 0.11372 | 0.11184 | -0.00188 |
| Advantage accuracy | 0.76008 | 0.75698 | -0.00310 |

The model has 342,279 parameters, of which 75,125 residual/router parameters
were trainable. Epoch 0 reproduced all recorded K=80 metrics with a maximum
absolute difference of `1.06e-7`. These numbers validate the implementation but
remain insufficient for a paper claim until multi-seed and held-out test runs.
